# CQ 21: Which data units of a case sit at which layer?
#
# Clause 5.6 places a data unit at the layer that formed it, and a refined
# model shows the same payload appearing once per layer it passes through.
#
# Restricted to the units a case reaches: those a communication transmits, and
# those a transmitted unit is built from or maps onto. The catalogue supplies
# the named kinds per layer, frame, packet, segment and the rest, and those say
# what a unit at a layer is called rather than what a communication carried.
#
# The reachable set is collected in one property path rather than in a union of
# class patterns. A union whose branches bind the unit by its class alone would
# match every individual of that class, the catalogue included, since nothing
# in such a branch ties it to the transmission.
#
# Test case 2 is the one that answers in full, having refined its architecture
# down to the three lower layers.
PREFIX iso7498: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#>
PREFIX rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?layerNumber ?dataUnit ?kind
WHERE {
  ?communication iso7498:transmits
    /(iso7498:hasUserData|iso7498:hasControlInformation|iso7498:mapsToServiceDataUnit)* ?u .
  ?u a ?class . ?class rdfs:subClassOf* iso7498:DataUnit .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?u a ?narrower . ?narrower rdfs:subClassOf+ ?class }
  OPTIONAL { ?u iso7498:atLayer/iso7498:layerNumber ?layerNumber }
  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?class), ".*#", "") AS ?kind)
  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?u),     ".*#", "") AS ?dataUnit)
} ORDER BY DESC(?layerNumber) ?dataUnit
